WEBVTT

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:19.950
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:19.950
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:19.950
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:46.720
Silver-White Valley

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:46.720
Chapter 1

00:01:58.310 --> 00:01:59.290
Why ?

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.960
Why can't I visit
him in his sickbed ?

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:09.840
His Majesty has only caught a
minor cold, so it's nothing serious.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.680
And since Countess
Grünewald is by his side...

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.350
...he says there's no need for
you to make a sickbed visit.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:20.750
He says I'm not needed ?

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.220
That's not quite
what he means, but...

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.590
That woman...

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:27.410
It all began when
that woman arrived.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.470
She's just a wench from
a poor aristocratic family.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.810
How dare she call herself
"Countess Grünewald."

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:35.590
She's put His Majesty
under her spell.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:40.090
If we let her be, she'll surely become
the bane of the Imperial Family.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.750
From what I know...

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.990
...it's not likely that Countess Grünewald
would ask for favors from His Majesty.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.000
This is what I've heard.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:57.750
I hear that woman's younger brother recently
graduated from Military Preparatory School...

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.250
...and whereas its graduates are
usually appointed Junior Ensigns...

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:03.930
...he was appointed an Ensign
as per His Majesty's order.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:10.060
That woman must have
begged His Majesty for it.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:14.060
Well, I heard
about that, too...

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:19.060
...but that brother of hers volunteered
to be assigned to front line duty.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:23.650
It doesn't seem like he merely wanted a
comfortable assignment or worldly fame.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:26.520
That's what he
wants us to think !

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.340
How cunning of that brat !

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.550
I suppose that
could be the case.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.180
That's it.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.290
That brat...

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.320
Yes ?

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.500
Let's kill that brat.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:42.950
We can't take any action
against that woman at Court.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:46.900
But it's convenient that her
brother is on the front lines.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.880
On the front lines,
he could die in battle.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:54.980
If that happens, I'll get to see that
woman lament and writhe in pain !

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:59.890
But I wonder if the enemy
will kill him so conveniently.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:02.220
We can make it easier
for that to happen.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:08.140
And if that doesn't work, bullets
don't always come from in front.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.110
That is how it is.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:16.860
Glaser, find out where that brat is assigned, and take appropriate measures.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.000
I don't care how
much it costs.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.480
Understand ?

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.350
Yes, Madam.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.160
How scary...

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.390
...a woman's
blind vengeance is.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:31.300
Even though I'm a woman
myself, it scares me.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.810
I suppose it
can't be helped.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:37.980
At one point, it was rumored
she would become Empress.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:43.280
But her first child was stillborn,
and then she had two miscarriages.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:49.120
These days, His Majesty's favor has
essentially shifted to Countess Grünewald.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:52.300
I suppose she can't console
herself about her misfortune...

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:55.890
...except by bearing a grudge
against Countess Grünewald.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:05:01.750
Still, her expression when she said she wanted
to see "that woman lament and writhe in pain"...

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.450
...it sent shivers down my spine.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:09.650
Though it may not seem that way now, when
she first came to the Court eleven years ago...

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:14.000
...she was such a gracious young lady that we
couldn't help but feel sympathetic toward her.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:19.060
I suppose women change.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:24.340
You do know that it is men's fault
that women change, Doctor ?

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.910
I found the file on
Countess Grünewald's brother.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.850
You found it ?

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:38.780
The Countess's brother, Ensign
Reinhard von Musel is to be assigned...

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:44.480
...to a front line base on
Planet Kapche-Lanka, B-III.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:48.390
Planet Kapche-Lanka...

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.680
Ensign Reinhard von Musel
reporting for duty.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:11.540
Junior Ensign Siegfried
Kircheis reporting for duty.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.540
You're the brother
of Countess Grünewald ?

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:19.990
Yes, sir.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:34.650
Even though His Majesty
favors your sister...

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:37.860
...you're no more than a
newly appointed Ensign.

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:39.750
Be sure to understand
your position...

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:43.000
...and don't do things that would
make others frown upon you.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.950
I understand.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:48.050
It looks like you graduated first in your
class from Military Preparatory School...

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:52.110
...but actual combat doesn't always
unfold according to school theory.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.250
Of course,
you'll learn that soon.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:54.880
Yes, sir.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.140
I'll keep
that in mind.

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:02.400
You may go.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.730
What do you think
of Captain Herder ?

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:19.100
There aren't many
competent people.

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:24.750
A superior who feigns austerity by making a 
speech that utterly lacks any sense of imagination...

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:27.070
...isn't worthy of respect.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:28.780
That's how it is.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:32.300
I think you're right, but...

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.190
But really...

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:46.130
But really, it's regrettable that the site
of my first battle is on a fringe planet.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:50.880
Since it's front line duty, it's at least better
than your initial prospective assignment.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:56.780
Rear-line duty. Even worse, 
an desk job in a military hospital !

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:58.750
How dare they mock me !

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:02.650
From the Human Resources Department's perspective it was their way of showing consideration.

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:07.600
After all, they didn't want to put Countess Grünewald's brother on the front lines and put his life at risk.

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:11.730
That's what I mean by
small-minded ways of thinking.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.290
We have big ambitions !

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:17.110
No way would I want to be thought of in the
same way as other aristocrats' children.

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:20.660
But we can't let
other people know that.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:24.800
For now, we should be glad that we
were able to get out to the front lines.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.110
You're right.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:30.410
But what in the world is the
battle on this planet about ?

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:35.000
There's an abundance of natural resources
here, so they don't want the enemy to have it.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.510
Both sides think that way...

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:39.550
...so each time the enemy builds a
development plant, they attack and destroy it.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:41.100
And they repeat
it over and over.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.880
There's no strategic importance.
It's a useless battle.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.710
You're right.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.340
But since this
is the front lines...

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.220
...we'll have a chance to
garner battlefield accolades.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:57.900
Please think of it as one step
on the way to our greater ambition.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:03.650
Kircheis, you're the type of person
who finds beauty even in trash.

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:08.130
If you hadn't met me and had instead
become a teacher or something...

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:10.750
...you might have become a great teacher
who finds a talent in each student...

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.420
...and encourages them
to make good use of it.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:28.750
If I hadn't met Lord
Reinhard and Lady Annerose...

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:36.130
"Siegfried" is a common name.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.830
But I like your
surname, Kircheis.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.480
It's very poetic.

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:47.210
So I'm going to
call you "Kircheis."

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:52.910
Sieg, please be a good
friend to my brother.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:39.830
Father, you sold Sister !

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.050
My brother can't go
to your school anymore.

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:58.780
It was just a short while,
but thank you for everything.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:34.370
Shut up !

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:47.110
What is it ?

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:49.030
A new recruit brat ?

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:51.020
We can pass her
down to you, if you want.

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:55.210
Of course, that's if you
can keep it up till then.

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:57.400
He probably can't.

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.970
Young guys are
always "quick," after all.

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:03.100
He probably can't keep it up.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:17.050
Stop it !

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:23.790
Did you hear that,
fellow soldiers ?

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:28.130
This red-haired boy
ordered us to stop.

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:33.420
We're so overwhelmed with shame.

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:38.340
I said stop it !

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:40.650
Here.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:58.350
You bastard.

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:02.190
This isn't a
joke, you know ?

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:09.150
Bastard !

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:10.220
We're going to kill you !

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:16.100
Now we've got you.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:37.070
Don't move.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:41.880
If you even flinch, I'll
crush your boss's throat.

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.480
If you're okay with that,
go ahead and make a move.

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:56.800
Kircheis, if any of them go
for their guns, shoot them.

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:58.740
I'll take responsibility for this.

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:07.640
What're you doing there ?!

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:21.150
Junior Ensign Kircheis,
although newly appointed...

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:25.000
...is of a higher rank than
they are, and his order was just.

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:28.100
The fault is solely theirs.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.930
Even though they are
soldiers of the Empire...

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:36.500
...they did something that dishonored
His Majesty and the Imperial Force.

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:41.200
Junior Ensign Kircheis tried
to rectify their wrongdoing...

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:45.410
...and to restore the trust
the people place in the military.

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:47.350
His actions are deserving of praise;
there's no reason to censure him.

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:52.640
But there's still the fact that he
participated in a brawl inside the base.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:57.390
Moreover, we hear that Junior Ensign
Kircheis is the one who threw the first punch.

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:01.350
I'm holding him responsible for the fact that
he caused a disturbance inside the base.

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:06.000
If you'll excuse me, but if the problem is
the disturbance of order inside the base...

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:09.850
...what you should truly be concerned
about is the lack of military discipline.

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:12.000
They abducted a civilian woman
from the mining plant...

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:16.460
...which the military is supposed to
protect, and attempted to assault her.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:18.800
According to military law,
that is a serious offense...

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:23.940
...for which they
could be shot on sight.

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:26.270
In Military Preparatory School,
they taught us to be firm...

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:30.350
...in dealing with those who
disturb military discipline.

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:33.460
But I suppose that doesn't work
according to theory on the front lines ?

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.730
You're going too far, Ensign !

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:38.060
I apologize, sir.

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:48.110
In any case, I can't listen
to just one side of the story.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:52.500
As for Junior Ensign Kircheis's punishment,
we'll let you know at a later time.

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:53.830
You may go.

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:09.770
How cheeky of
you, blond brat !

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:13.290
You think bullets only
come from in front ?

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:15.860
You think so, too ?

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:23.980
Captain, if we let a rebellious kid
like him do whatever he wants...

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:29.210
...it'll become an issue of the maintaining
of order, and furthermore, of your authority.

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:31.000
Shouldn't we do
something about him ?

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:34.800
This is...?

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:36.890
Read it.

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:42.100
It's a secret letter from someone who's been
given an order by someone of noble rank.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.390
A secret letter...?

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:55.750
Lord Reinhard, I'm
sorry about the trouble.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:58.930
Why are you apologizing ?

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.070
You did the right thing.

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:05.210
But it put you in a
difficult situation.

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:12.050
If I'd been the one who'd witnessed
it first and hadn't tried to save her...

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:14.900
...you'd have contempt
for me, wouldn't you ?

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.310
It's the same thing.

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:17.400
Don't worry about it.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:18.320
Thank you.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.590
I said don't
worry about it.

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:23.450
If you keep bowing your head
for something like this...

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:26.400
...you'll eventually have
to walk on your hands.

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:33.950
This is...!

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:37.180
That's how it is, Lieutenant.

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:42.450
This someone wants the death of
the one you call the blond brat.

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:44.950
But, Captain...

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:51.510
Lieutenant, you know,
I hate this planet.

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:57.120
I've always wanted to be assigned where there's
less danger if an opportunity would present itself.

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:58.050
How about you ?

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.040
Well...

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:06.750
This is the "opportunity"
that's presented itself.

00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:10.090
Don't you think ?

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.030
I think so.

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:19.610
Yes, I believe so !

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:25.330
Then that makes two of us.

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:27.160
What do you think we
should do about it ?

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:33.460
But, Captain, that brat is still the
brother of Countess Grünewald.

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.560
We can't kill him
with our own hands.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:37.340
Of course not.

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:41.610
If we do that, we'll be done for, regardless
of whether or not we have a backer.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:47.180
So, he wants
battlefield accolades.

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:51.150
Why not give him the opportunity
to make his dream come true ?

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:54.610
I see.

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:59.820
Then an outcome that isn't necessarily
what he wants might come about.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:02.500
Is that how it is ?

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:09.980
Yeah.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:16.180
Besides, a commander who can't rectify the
lapse of military discipline is incompetent !

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:17.150
Now...

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:23.700
I will relay an order
from the Commander.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:29.680
Ensign Reinhard von Musel and
Junior Ensign Siegfried Kircheis...

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:33.750
...at 08:00 tomorrow you will
use a mobile armored vehicle...

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.350
...and undertake the task of
reconnoitering the enemy's movement.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.270
Just the two of us ?

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:40.230
Yes.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.270
Are you dissatisfied...

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:45.650
...or scared ?

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:47.900
No, I accept the order.

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:49.770
We'll immediately
prepare for the mission.

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:58.860
What a useless provocation.

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:03.750
Since we're unfamiliar with the region, and no guide will accompany us, that means...

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:07.650
It's clearly intended
to be a punishment.

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:11.500
But if we're lucky
and a battle takes place...

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.750
...it'll be the two of us alone
who'll achieve distinction.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:15.340
I look forward to that.

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:18.630
Lord Reinhard is
always like that.

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:22.960
Reinhard !

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:26.930
I'm going to
join the military.

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:29.460
That way, I can be
on my own faster.

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:32.900
I want to climb up the
ladder and liberate my sister.

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:36.990
Hey, Kircheis, why don't you come
with me to Military Preparatory School ?

00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:42.910
Okay ?

00:21:53.810 --> 00:21:54.880
Kircheis.

00:21:56.940 --> 00:21:59.790
Our battle finally begins.

00:22:01.100 --> 00:22:02.310
Lord Reinhard...

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:08.280
We'll fight, we'll win,
we'll continue to win...

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:11.570
...and we'll get my sister
back no matter what.

00:22:11.570 --> 00:22:12.630
Yes.

00:22:13.400 --> 00:22:16.140
Until that day comes,
we'll never lose.

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:18.690
No matter who the enemy is.

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:21.470
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:22:27.750 --> 00:22:34.120
Space Year 791,
Imperial Year 482, July...

00:22:37.510 --> 00:22:41.920
...Reinhard von Musel
and Siegfried Kircheis...

00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:47.200
...their long, long history
of battles was about to begin.

00:22:45.150 --> 00:22:48.800
To be continued

00:22:51.650 --> 00:22:59.000
Reinhard:

00:22:51.650 --> 00:22:59.000
Horikawa Ryo

00:22:59.750 --> 00:23:07.050
Benemunde:

00:22:59.750 --> 00:23:07.050
Fujita Toshiko

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:15.120
Narrator:

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:15.120
Yara Yuusaku

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:26.800
Pour the light into the night sky, a mystic silver curtain

00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:25.350
[ Explanations ]

00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:25.350
Ending Theme

00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:25.350
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:25.350
Written by: Ogura Kei

00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:31.600
The dance of the entire firmament, the mystery of the aurora

00:23:30.210 --> 00:23:35.190
Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:31.890 --> 00:23:36.160
I believe explanations for those will be given some day

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:41.190
Timing:
Todd Perkins

00:23:37.550 --> 00:23:47.600
Even the mystery of this life that it is, some day...

00:23:41.190 --> 00:23:47.200
Song Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:53.400
Editing:
Todd Perkins
Barbara
Dave
Brain
Mouse
Omar
Steve S.
Horus

00:23:47.750 --> 00:23:52.150
...from something to something to be created, to be born -

00:23:52.350 --> 00:23:57.050
Someone will give us an explanation for how that happens

00:23:53.400 --> 00:24:03.360
Subtitled by:
Central Anime(Kansas)

00:23:58.030 --> 00:24:07.200
It is something that intelligent people will figure out

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:12.600
But the answer given to me when I ask "Why ?"...

00:24:12.900 --> 00:24:17.700
...is usually just a formulaic one

00:24:17.980 --> 00:24:22.990
What in the world is that worth ?

00:24:23.150 --> 00:24:30.050
If I ask, they only hesitate to answer

00:24:30.850 --> 00:24:40.850
Why you came to love me isn't something you need to explain

00:24:41.150 --> 00:24:53.750
Those eyes in which the auroras flutter can simply remain a mystery

00:25:11.540 --> 00:25:16.500
Preview of Next Episode

00:25:17.370 --> 00:25:19.250
As per Captain
Herder's orders...

00:25:19.250 --> 00:25:22.510
...Reinhard and Kircheis go out
on reconnaissance by themselves.

00:25:22.510 --> 00:25:26.450
Regardless of the circumstances, they're
excited about their long-awaited first battle.

00:25:26.450 --> 00:25:29.350
But there, a villainous
trap awaits them.

00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:32.100
Next episode...

00:25:31.650 --> 00:25:41.730
Legend of the Galactic Heroes Gaiden

00:25:31.650 --> 00:25:41.730
Chapter 2

00:25:31.650 --> 00:25:41.730
Silver-White Valley

00:25:36.470 --> 00:25:39.900
My friend, do you remember
those days on the battlefield ?
